response:
Computing the angle $\theta$ in this problem is much like computing the angle between the normals of the planes. So we take the vectors $\mathbf A = \langle 2, 1, -2 \rangle$ and $\mathbf B = \langle 6, 3, 2 \rangle$ corresponding to the coefficients in each plane, and compute the angle between them. We have $$ \cos \theta = \frac{6 + 3 - 4}{\sqrt{4 + 1 + 4} \; \sqrt{36 + 9 + 4}}
= \frac{5}{\sqrt{69} \cdot \sqrt{49}} 
= \frac{5}{7\sqrt{69}}.$$
<end think>

